1282 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 359 0 R/E(The pedestrian network was modeled using a walking speed of 4 km/h , based on a simplified version of Tobler\220s hiking function, which accounts for average slope conditions. Given that most of the area is located on a hill , this has a direct impact on movement patterns, as slopes tend to reduce walking speeds, especially in steeper sections. As a result, travel times on foot increase in these elevated zones, affecting overall accessibility and shaping the spatial distribution of reachable services within the neighborhood.)/Pg 37 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

